Common settings (run_MPC.py and run_MPC_no_V.py)
=================================================

Finite horizon: 12 h (1 cycle)
Sampling time: 1 h
Demand cycle: 12 h, sinusoidal, +/-5%
Simulation period: 120 h

Initial condition:
  state/reference file = css_41.xlsx
  infinite-tail default pressure = 55 bar
  unfix_P_at_t0 = True
  compressor_P at t = 0 is unfixed during controller initialization
  and before every MPC controller solve

Infinite-domain mapping: gamma = 0.1
Discretization: LAGRANGE-RADAU
Infinite finite elements: NFE = 10
Collocation points per element: NCP = 4
Compressor power collocation points: reduced to 1 per element
Tail integration: composite Radau quadrature; singular tau = 1 point omitted

Link finite and infinite horizons:
  intermediate pipe pressure p
  compressor power P

Terminal constraints:
  hard equality for intermediate pipe pressure p
  hard equality for compressor power P
  no terminal rho constraint
  no terminal slack/penalty (terminal_cost = 0)

Infinite mass-balance differential equation:
  inactive at tau = 0 and tau = 1

Dynamic source boundary conditions:
  source_1 pressure = 35.01325 bar
  source_2 pressure = 35.01325 bar
  source_3 flow fixed at its initial value

IPOPT tolerance: 1e-4
IPOPT linear solver: ma57


run_MPC.py (with Lyapunov stability constraint)
================================================

Lyapunov tracking variables:
  intermediate pipe pressure p
  compressor ratio beta

CSS tail reference: closest integer CSS point; no interpolation
Stability constraint: enabled
Lyapunov decrease factor: delta = 0.1

Output:
  Inf.xlsx
  Inf.txt
  Excel includes objective, Lyapunov, and runtime sheets


run_MPC_no_V.py (without Lyapunov stability constraint)
=======================================================

No Lyapunov tracking expressions
No Lyapunov decrease constraint
No plant tracking cost
No Lyapunov result sheet

Output:
  Inf_no_V.xlsx
  Inf_no_V.txt
  Excel includes objective and runtime sheets
